{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'gh pr view 977 --repo endojs/endo-but-for-bots --json body --jq .body'","aggregated_output":"## Description\n\nThis PR pins the daemon's intended Host/Guest authority boundary with a live-daemon regression test.\n\nThe test provisions an actual guest through `provideGuest`, compares its CapTP method surface with the Host surface, and asserts that all 40 Host-only methods remain absent. It then deliberately oversteps the `EndoGuest` type and calls `makeUnconfinedFromTree`, `makeUnconfined`, `makeArchive`, `makeFromTree`, `stageTree`, `endow`, and `provideHost`; every call is rejected at the CapTP receiver because the method does not exist. It also follows the guest's reserved `@host` pet name and confirms that the resulting parent mail handle cannot recover `makeUnconfinedFromTree`.\n\nThis establishes the behavior of a correctly constructed `EndoGuest`. A separate deployment-path investigation is ongoing privately and is deliberately not described in this public PR.\n\n### Security Considerations\n\nThe regression prevents the daemon's guest facet or interface guard from silently gaining Host-only methods. It does not claim that every external gateway necessarily serves a guest facet; that integration boundary is outside this change and is under separate review.\n\n### Scaling Considerations\n\nThe regression starts one daemon and adds no production cost.\n\n### Documentation Considerations\n\nNo user-facing API or runtime behavior changes.\n\n### Testing Considerations\n\n- Full `packages/daemon/test/endo.test.js`: 228 tests passed. A temporary, uncommitted short socket directory was used because the isolated job worktree path exceeds the Unix-domain socket length limit.\n- Package TypeScript check passed.\n- Target-file Prettier and ESLint checks passed (pre-existing warnings only).\n- All deterministic pre-push probes passed.\n\nRegression evidence: I temporarily added `makeUnconfinedFromTree` to both `GuestInterface` and the guest exo. The new test failed on the complete Host-only surface assertion, identifying the leaked method. After reverting that deliberate break, the targeted test passed.\n\n### Compatibility Considerations\n\nTest-only. No changeset is needed.\n\n### Upgrade Considerations\n\nThis test-only PR does not change deployed runtime behavior. Deployment requirements depend on the separate private gateway investigation.\n\n<!-- garden-job: ebfb-guest-unconfined-from-tree -->\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
